// CROWN — a POSITIVE declared row is a CAP on the callbacks it invokes
// (A3-pos, 2026-09-27): `with E` on `run` says its body, callbacks
// included, performs at most E. The callback performs F, so the argument
// edge violates the cap. Accepted by boot d27fc81d, where a positive row
// installed no gate (only its negation half did).
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op_e() -> Int }
effect F { op_f() -> Int }
handler he { op_e() => resume(1) }
handler hf { op_f() => resume(10) }
fn run(f) with E = f() + op_e()
fn main() = (run(() => op_f())) ~> he ~> hf
